Create an intelligent customer support workspace that transforms unorganized customer messages into structured, trackable, and actionable support tickets.

The system should support three roles:

1. Administrator
2. Support Agent
3. Customer

Provide role-appropriate interfaces and permissions.

Administrator:

- View all tickets and agents.
- Manage support agents.
- Assign and reassign tickets.
- View analytics and reports.
- Configure ticket categories and priorities.
- Monitor performance and resolution times.

Support Agent:

- View assigned tickets.
- Accept tickets.
- Update ticket status.
- Respond to customers.
- View AI recommendations.
- Summarize conversations.
- Search similar resolved tickets.
- Track their own performance.

Customer:

- Create a support ticket.
- View their submitted tickets.
- Read support responses.
- Add messages to conversations.
- Track ticket progress.
- Reopen an eligible resolved ticket.

Implement authentication and authorization on the backend. Do not rely solely on hiding frontend components to enforce permissions.

For local development, provide a clearly documented way to create the first administrator account and demonstration accounts.

